  "schema": 1,
  "study": "Building Tunable CRDTs, André dos Reis Martins Rijo (2018), chapter 5 and Appendix E",
  "source": "https://run.unl.pt/server/api/core/bitstreams/d2570d62-6972-4877-a791-636d876d0096/content",
  "pdf_sha256": "193d967847376d802d4d60b4b64c5f6d39b27620839138f1ec5ecdd2a4bb1ef6",
  "source_scope": "Algorithms 5.3 and 5.4, Figures 5.7, 5.12 and E.1 define stamped issue, FIFO broadcast, and local histories. Figure 5.17 shows replica and element symmetry. The university ORIGINAL bundle lists just the PDF. The published implementation repository contains Java; an original executable Toolbox specification and a final TLC log for the three-element stop have not been identified. The reconstructed graph uses all three policies per operation kind and a unique stamp.",
  "authors_repository": "https://github.com/AndreRijo/T-CRDTs/tree/1792fbaa22c8f89cff4db5f886866b9795b9a7df",
  "author_results": {
    "hardware": "One node, two Xeon E5-2620 v2 CPUs, 64 GB RAM.",
    "key": "replicas, operations per replica, elements",
    "elapsed_s": {
      "2,2,1": 4,
      "2,2,2": 12,
      "2,2,3": 25,
      "2,3,1": 212,
      "2,3,2": 9780,
      "2,3,3": 55140,
      "3,2,1": 3506,
      "3,2,2": 208800
    },
    "3,2,3": "Stopped after approximately nine billion generated states and about 750 GB disk. Distinct count, depth and complete count unavailable."
  },
  "properties": "The reconstruction verifies FIFO history accounting and replica convergence of the underlying full operation sets. The counted graph covers the structural transition system. It does not evaluate the thesis’s complete history-replay predicate, policy conflict predicates or query definitions. No historical speedup claim.",
  "encoding": "State fields for own issued count, operation set, ordered receive/issue history, FIFO inbox, last received record, clock and control label. Done recovers finished. Kind and policy select the source policy pair; the fixed happens-before policy is implicit. Read-only queries do not constrain Next. Nonterminal empty receive and final PlusCal stutter are counted.",
  "platform": "Dedicated c7i.4xlarge in us-east-2, Xeon Platinum 8488C, Linux 7.0.0-1018-aws. Explicit Core and TLC each used one physical core on the control panel; the source counter ran in a fresh Python process pinned to CPU 1. Wall seconds and peak process RSS use GNU time. External setup excluded.",
  "commands": {
    "counter": "python3 scripts/perf/scale/tunable_set_counts.py R N E P [--symmetry]",
    "cfg": "Repeat the counter command with --emit-config and redirect stdout to model.cfg.",
    "core": "dive check TunableSetHistory.tla --config model.cfg --store exact --workers 1 --compat=tlc --seed 0 --fp 0 --time-limit 130s --max-memory 6g --output json",
    "tlc": "java -Xmx4g -XX:ActiveProcessorCount=1 -cp tla2tools.jar tlc2.TLC -workers 1 -fp 0 -seed 0 -metadir FRESH -config model.cfg TunableSetHistory.tla"
  },
  "negative_controls": {
    "receive_order": "Add clock = MaxIssued to Receive. R=2,N=1,E=2,P=1, labeled. Core and TLC each find 521 distinct / 843 generated / depth 9, compared with 913 / 1467 / depth 9 in the original reconstruction. All queues exhausted.",
    "missing_history": "On Receive replace append(history, x) by <<x>>. Both explicit checkers report HistoryAgreement, 50 distinct / 52 generated / depth 4 with 39 queued. The genuine four-state trace validates independently. Changing the initial clock to 1 fails independent Init at state zero.",
    "counter_admission": "Substituting the LateReceive module at the expected filename refused with exit 2. A one-creator-prefix budget also refused with exit 2 and emitted no partial count."
  },
  "independent_calculation": "A separate Burnside sum enumerated actor permutations, fixed-point payload colors and independent local histories. Both counters agreed for all 72 combinations of 1–3 replicas, 1–2 operations per replica, 1–3 elements, 1 or 3 policies per operation, and both symmetry choices.",
